{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He spoke, etc., saying.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>saying</b>, since the speech was only to Moses. Perhaps it comes to authorize him to say that these matters were spoken to him from the mouth of the Shekhinah — without this, he would be in violation of ״you shall not say״ (Yoma 4a). Also, so that Israel would not suspect him that Moses desired the matter, and say that his opinion was like theirs; therefore He commands him to tell them that the King so commanded him. Also, so that they would listen to him to send [spies] according to the order spoken to him from HaShem, and would not hold back through him when they know that it is the word of the King. Also, according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory, who explained the word ״for yourself״ — ״according to your judgment,״ meaning that HaShem does not command regarding the matter — HaShem desires that he say to Israel the matters exactly as they are, from the mouth of the Most High; perhaps they will sense that it is not a good thing to do, and they will trust in HaShem and believe in Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:15.117158379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}